th must first lose a diamond trick. West is likely to have the @DQ for his opening bid and South should use avoidance technique so that only West can win a diamond trick for the defense. A diamond is led toward dummy at trick 3 and, when West follows small, South must win the trick in dummy. "],["pg",""],["ls","sd"],["ls","wd"],["ls","nd"],["pc","d"],["pc","d"],["pc","dk"],["pc","d"],["pg",""],["hs","nc"],["hs","sc"],["nt","South crosses to the closed hand in clubs "],["pg",""],["ls","nc"],["ls","sc"],["pc","c"],["pc","c"],["pc","ck"],["pc","c"],["pg",""],["hs","sd"],["hs","wd"],["hs","nd"],["at","to play another diamond toward dummy. West must play the @DQ this time (or it will be easy to endplay him with that card) and South allows West to hold this trick. "],["pg",""],["ls","wd"],["ls","nd"],["ls","sd"],["pc","d"],["pc","dq"],["pc","d"],["pc","d"],["pg",""],["hs","wd"],["hs","nd"],["at","West returns a diamond to the dummy (as good as anything). "],["pg",""],["ls","wd"],["ls","nd"],["pc","d"],["pc","d"],["pc","d"],["pc","d"],["pg",""],["hs","nh"],["hs","sh"],["at","South should cash his remaining heart winner "],["pg",""],["ls","nh"],["ls","sh"],["pc","h"],["pc","h"],["pc","h"],["pc","h"],["pg",""],["hs","nc"],["hs","sc"],["at","and finish the clubs ending in dummy (the @C6 and @C5 must be unblocked). "],["pg",""],["ls","nc"],["ls","sc"],["pc","c6"],["pc","c"],["pc","ca"],["pc","c"],["pg",""],["pc","cq"],["pc","c"],["pc","c5"],["pc","s"],["pg",""],["pc","c"],["pc","h"],["pc","c"],["hs","ws"],["nt","West is caught in a ^*B1-suit squeeze^*N on the fourth round of clubs. "],["pg",""],["at","If West retains a small spade, "],["pg",""],["ls","ws"],["pc","sj"],["pg",""],["hs","ns"],["hs","es"],["at","a spade is led from the dummy and East must play the @S10 (or else South would duck to endplay West). "],["pg",""],["ls","ns"],["ls","es"],["pc","s"],["pc","st"],["hs","ss"],["hs","ws"],["at","South covers with the @SK and West wins the @SA. "],["pg",""],["ls","ss"],["ls",